<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<locale-config xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!--
      The languages the interface is actually translated into. Every locale named here has a complete
      `values-<locale>/` translation of the UI strings, because declaring a language whose resources do
      not exist offers a per-app language setting that changes nothing - the app would sit in the
      picker and stay English. An earlier revision of this file named English alone for that reason;
      the translations now exist, so the list is real rather than aspirational.

      Adding a locale here without adding its `values-<locale>/` directory is the defect this comment
      exists to prevent. `scripts/verify.mjs` checks the two agree.

      Translation is not a fallback chain: a string missing from one locale falls back to English
      per-string, so a partial translation degrades to English words rather than to a blank or a crash.
      That is why every locale below is complete rather than best-effort.

      Languages deliberately not offered yet, in the order they would be added next: Arabic (needs a
      right-to-left layout pass, not just strings), Hindi, Indonesian, Vietnamese, Korean, Thai.
    -->
    <locale android:name="en" />
    <locale android:name="ru" />
    <locale android:name="de" />
    <locale android:name="fr" />
    <locale android:name="es" />
    <locale android:name="pt" />
    <locale android:name="it" />
    <locale android:name="nl" />
    <locale android:name="pl" />
    <locale android:name="tr" />
    <locale android:name="ja" />
    <locale android:name="zh-CN" />
</locale-config>
